# The home skeleton's font preference: a fresh home is seeded with this
# the first time its owner logs in (the session's init copies it in if the
# home has none), so a new user starts with a font layer of their own that
# they can edit — the per-user accessibility scale. It merges over the
# system layer (conf/font.msh) in fontsvc: here only `scale` is set, so the
# system's sizes and families carry through and every program's type grows
# together. Ships larger than 1.0 so the per-user push is visible on first
# login; a user who wants the system size sets `scale: 1.0` (or empties it).
{
  scale: 1.5
}
